From: zerogap
Subject: keyboard: Brazilian ABNT2 keymap, switched at run time

zerogap's keyboard layout is a setting (zerogap.txt "keyboard", and while
running: src/kbdindev.cpp), so the keymap can change after the keyboard
is attached: CUSBKeyboardDevice::SetKeyMap() and CKeyMap::LoadMap().

ABNT2 ("BR") has a key at HID usage 0x87 (International1, "/ ?"), above
the old PHY_MAX_CODE (127), and Circle's cooked mode took the key codes
0x80-0x87 for the modifier keys: that key acted as a held right Windows
key. The modifiers now use their HID usages (0xE0-0xE7) and the maps go
up to 0x87 (the other maps' missing rows are KeyNone).

Its dead keys (´ ` ~ ^ ¨) give their spacing accents (Latin-1);
src/kbdindev.cpp composes them with the next key. Caps Lock also changes
the case of Latin-1 letters (ç, á...).

diff --git a/include/circle/input/keymap.h b/include/circle/input/keymap.h
--- a/include/circle/input/keymap.h
+++ b/include/circle/input/keymap.h
@@ -22,7 +22,7 @@
 
 #include <circle/types.h>
 
-#define PHY_MAX_CODE	127
+#define PHY_MAX_CODE	0x87		// zerogap: up to International1 (ABNT2's / ?)
 
 #define K_NORMTAB	0
 #define K_SHIFTTAB	1
@@ -130,6 +130,10 @@
 
 	u8 GetLEDStatus (void) const;
 
+	// zerogap: switches to one of the built-in maps ("US", "BR", ...),
+	// keeping Caps Lock and Num Lock. FALSE: no such map, nothing changed.
+	boolean LoadMap (const char *pLocale);
+
 private:
 	static const void *LookupDefaultMap (const char *pLocale);
 
